#: ../../../policy/CMP0234.rst:2
msgid "CMP0234"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0234.rst:6
msgid ""
"MSVC conformant preprocessor is controlled by :prop_tgt:`C_EXTENSIONS` "
"and :prop_tgt:`CXX_EXTENSIONS`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0234.rst:9
msgid ""
"The :prop_tgt:`C_EXTENSIONS` and :prop_tgt:`CXX_EXTENSIONS` target "
"properties select whether compiler-specific language extensions are "
"enabled.  The ``MSVC`` compiler uses its traditional preprocessor by "
"default, regardless of those properties.  Visual Studio 2019 version 16.5 "
"and above offer the ``/Zc:preprocessor`` flag to select the standard-"
"conforming preprocessor, and ``/Zc:preprocessor-`` to select the traditional "
"one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0234.rst:16
msgid ""
"In CMake 4.5 and below, :prop_tgt:`C_EXTENSIONS` "
"and :prop_tgt:`CXX_EXTENSIONS` had no influence on the preprocessor.  CMake "
"4.6 and above prefer to pass ``/Zc:preprocessor`` when compiler extensions "
"are disabled.  This policy provides compatibility for projects that have not "
"been updated to expect the behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0234.rst:22
msgid ""
"The ``OLD`` behavior for this policy does not add ``/Zc:preprocessor``. The "
"``NEW`` behavior adds ``/Zc:preprocessor`` or ``/Zc:preprocessor-`` where "
"appropriate for the extensions settings of the target.  The flags are placed "
"before the target's :prop_tgt:`COMPILE_OPTIONS`.  The :ref:`Visual Studio "
"Generators` compile the C and C++ sources of a target with one set of "
"options, so for consistent behavior across generators a target that uses "
"both languages is handled as a whole.  If :prop_tgt:`C_EXTENSIONS` "
"and :prop_tgt:`CXX_EXTENSIONS` differ for such a target, the conformant "
"preprocessor is used for both languages, as if the extensions were disabled "
"for both."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0234.rst:33
msgid ""
"The policy setting is recorded by each target when it is created.  It is "
"also propagated to the test projects of the :command:`try_compile` "
"and :command:`try_run` commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0234.rst:37
msgid ""
"This policy has no effect on other languages, on compilers other than "
"``MSVC``, or on versions of it that do not support the flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/include/STANDARD_ADVICE.rst:1
msgid ""
"This policy was introduced in CMake version |INTRODUCED_IN_CMAKE_VERSION|. "
"It may be set by :command:`cmake_policy` "
"or :command:`cmake_minimum_required`. If it is not set, CMake |"
"WARNS_OR_DOES_NOT_WARN|, and uses ``OLD`` behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/include/DEPRECATED.rst:2
msgid ""
"The ``OLD`` behavior of a policy is :ref:`deprecated by definition <cmake-"
"policies-intro>` and may be removed in a future version of CMake."
msgstr ""
